Subject: [PATCH] syncservice: optional oldest-first initial sync for date-ordered UIDs

Applied by proton-bridge-gtk to the pinned upstream tag; not an upstream change.

Gluon assigns UIDs in the order messages are applied, and the upstream initial
sync walks the API from the newest message to the oldest, so UID 1 is the newest
message. Clients such as Geary treat a higher UID as newer mail.

Only when BRIDGE_GTK_SYNC_OLDEST_FIRST=1 is set, the metadata iterator collects
the complete metadata list with the unchanged Desc/EndID paging, sorts it by
(Time, ID) ascending and feeds the unchanged pipeline. Its resume cursor is kept
in LastSyncedMessageID with an "oldest-first:v1:" prefix; a cursor written in the
other mode is rejected so that a mode change requires a full repair.
Without the variable, behaviour is identical to upstream.

---
